1.  An Introduction
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  IPLRead was written because I recently decided to upgrade my BBS to
Excelsior!  BBS.  The thing with Excelsior, is that it doesn't use
standard ANSI codes for the menus and text screens.  It uses a system
called IPL (Intuitive Programming Language), which is a variant of the
standard MCI codes, which uses the "\" character as an identifier for the
start of a code.

  This makes designing screens and such forth quite hard, as the text is
all over the place.  It also means that you can only check what it will
look like from withen Excelsior.


  Therefore, IPLRead simply translates the IPL codes into ANSI and either
displays the file to the console or saves it to disk.



2.  Requirments
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  IPLRead can only be used on machine with at least V37 of the DOS library
(seeing as Excelsior only works with V37+ I decided not to provide support
for < V35 ).



3.  Usage
~~~~~~~~~
  IPLRead can only be used from the CLI/SHELL.  The arguments available
are:  NAME/A,TO/K,F=FILTER/S

  NAME - This is the name of the text file to display.  It can be any text
file (all ANSI and standard ASCII is supported as well as IPL codes).
This is ALWAYS required otherwise nothing will happen

  TO - This is an optional filename.  If none is specified, then the text
file will just be typed to the console.  If a file name is present, then
the file will be saved out to disk.

  F=FILTER - The optional flag is the FILTER option.  After the file
name, you can place a F or the word FILTER, and ALL IPL codes will be
filtered out of the file.  This can make the file look strange, especially
if there are codes like the ones to display variables and clear the screen
and such forth.  This option was mainly added so that the Excelsior! log
files would be more readable.


  Unfortunally, not all of the IPL codes are supported in this version of
IPLRead.  Hopefully, I will include the missing functions in later
releases.  The commands that are available are:

   Bx     Print x bells (DisplayBeep() on local console)
   Cx     Change the cursor color to:
   Fx     Screen Manipulation, move cursor to:
   Hn     Print x backspaces
   Nx     Print x newlines
   Ox     Set BOLD Text (ANSI)
   Qx     IPL Setting Mode:
   Rx     Set Reverse Mode:
   Ux     Set underline mode
   Vx     Display a system variable. Replaces variable with description
   Xx     Immediatedly exit message
   Zn     Change background color, use same colors as command "C"
   ^x     Move cursor up x lines
   !x     Move cursor down x lines
   >x     Move cursor right x columns
   <x     Move cursor left x columns
   \\     Actually print a single slash "\"
   \      A slash on it's own (end of some IPL commands)


  Also, with some of the control codes, like Bold, Underline, I use the
ANSI code to turn off the setting, whereas Excelsior!  appears to just
send a Reset code (<esc>[0m).  Therefore is something looks good using
IPLRead, please check it via Excelsior!  just to make sure.  I guess they
had to do it this way so it works with all terminals that support ANSI.



4.  History
~~~~~~~~~~~
V1.00   6 January 93
    * First release.

V1.01   7 January 93
    * Corrected error with Newlines & Backspaces.  Would output too many
      due to typo in Number conversion routine
    * Improved IPL converson routines
    * Added support for more than single digit numbers for all IPL codes
      that make use of them
    * Increased IPL translation buffer size (now 4 times original size)

V1.02   7 January 93
    * Corrected Error with copy loops
    * Changed from normal Write() to VFPrintf()   (buffered write)
    * Added TO option, so files can be saved to disk instead of just being
      viewed
    * Changed back from using CSI code ($9B) to using <esc>[ to make
      editing in text editors (like CED) a lot easier
    * Added break option (CTRL-C)

V1.03   24 January 93
    * Corrected error with change of background colour routine
    * Now supports \ on it's own (some IPL commands need this as an end of
      command identifier)
    * Cleaned up code and text slightly

V1.04   28 January 93
    * Now should always work.  Used to stop after typing the first line of
      text.  Couldn't guess why, but hopefully this has fixed it.
    * Removed ANSI-code to activate Console wordwraping.  This should make
      things works a little faster.
    * Removed an old routine that was no-longer being called, but still
      existed in the final file.

V1.05   28 January 93
    * Re-wrote Load/Save routines so it should work correctly.  Was still
      not working on Renze's system even after my last attack at the code.
    * Added two more IPL variables.  \v@ (BBS Name) & \v# (UUCP Address)

V1.06   1 February 93
    * Changed to using PowerPacker.library by Nico François for file
      routines in the hope that would make things better.

V1.10   1 February 93
    * Removed PowerPacker routines as they were not helping.
    * Totally re-wrote the output routines.
    * Improved file error handling
    * Removed checks for \'s on their own, because it helps to point out
      any mistakes if they are removed properly.
    * Cleaned up conversion routines, thus increaseing overall speed.



